{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And he began to mention the punishment of those written at the beginning of the pericah, from the father, as in 'a man, his mother and his father, you shall fear.' And the reason the father is mentioned before the mother is on account of his honor, and it is not like 'a man, his mother and his father, you shall fear,' for he would not be put to death if he were not of legal age." "<b>Whoever curses his father.</b> It draws itself and another with it, and likewise 'and whoever curses his mother.' And the meaning of <b>his father and his mother he cursed</b> is as if saying: he has done a great abomination." "<b>His blood is in him.</b> Like 'his blood is on his head,' and likewise the stoned and the strangled, their blood is in them. And he says this as a general principle for all modes of execution, that we require the tradition of our fathers, for we cannot derive them to put them to death from the verse; also it is not written how many years old a boy must be to be of legal age."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:20.714643621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}